EF=formula('Δs=2πr Δn/N',{'Δs':'signed wheel travel','r':'wheel radius','Δn':'signed decoded encoder count increment','N':'decoded counts per complete wheel revolution after any gearbox and quadrature convention','π':'circle constant'},{'Δs,r':'m','Δn,N':'counts; count ratio dimensionless','π':'dimensionless'},['Added explicit calibration; ideal rolling; N>0. Do not apply a second ×4 factor when N already counts all decoded edges.'])
add([(1887,'statement','Encoder counts converted into wheel displacement; no numeric encoder specification printed.')],'counts','Encoder conversion','Added calibration: N=1200 decoded counts per wheel revolution, r=0.10 m and Δn=300 counts. What wheel travel is inferred?',['0.05π m, approximately 0.1571 m.','0.20π m, approximately 0.6283 m.','0.0125π m, approximately 0.0393 m.','0.025 m.'],'The wheel turns one quarter of a revolution, so travel is (300/1200)2π(0.10)=0.05π m.',['This uses a whole revolution instead of a quarter.','This applies an extra divide-by-four to an already decoded count calibration.','This omits the circumference factor 2π.'],typ='numerical',difficulty='medium',assumptions=['The specified N is wheel-side decoded counts per revolution; gearing and quadrature factors are already included.'],steps=['Compute fractional revolution 300/1200.','Multiply by wheel circumference 2πr.'],forms=[EF])
add([(1887,'statement','Errors accumulate from wheel slip and uneven terrain.')],'slip','Odometry drift','An encoder reports wheel rotation while the tyre slips on the floor. Which inference is justified?',['The no-slip conversion can overestimate actual ground travel, and accumulated pose drift can remain.','The count-to-distance formula automatically measures true ground displacement despite slip.','A higher count resolution alone removes all slip-induced pose error.','Wheel odometry becomes an absolute map-relative position measurement.'],'Wheel encoders measure rotation; slip breaks the assumed relationship to ground motion and can cause accumulated error.',['The geometric conversion depends on rolling assumptions.','Resolution does not remove the violated contact model.','Integrated wheel motion remains relative odometry, not an absolute map reference.'],typ='scenario')
add([(1888,'table','P present error, I accumulated error, D overshoot/stability role.')],'pid-roles','PID contributions','Which pairing follows the source PID table?',['P: present error; I: accumulated error; D: change-sensitive damping role.','P: accumulated error; I: present error; D: map construction.','P: wheel geometry; I: object classes; D: pose particles.','P: derivative error; I: PWM carrier frequency; D: error integral.'],'The source distinguishes proportional, integral and derivative roles in speed regulation.',['This swaps P/I and assigns mapping to D.','These are other robotics functions, not PID contributions.','This does not match the controller terms.'])
PF=formula('u=Kp e+Ki I+Kd (e−eprev)/Δt; I=Iprev+eΔt',{'u':'dimensionless normalized motor command before saturation','e,eprev':'current and previous desired-minus-measured wheel angular velocity error','I,Iprev':'current and previous discrete error integral','Δt':'sample interval','Kp':'proportional gain','Ki':'integral gain','Kd':'derivative gain'},{'u':'dimensionless','e,eprev':'rad/s','I,Iprev':'rad','Δt':'s','Kp':'s/rad','Ki':'1/rad','Kd':'s²/rad'},['Added rectangular integral/backward derivative convention; gains and initial integral explicitly supplied; no saturation in the arithmetic unless stated.'])
add([(1888,'table','PID terms and encoder-feedback regulation objectives.')],'pid-step','Added discrete PID step','Added discrete rule: I=Iprev+eΔt and u=Kp e+Ki I+Kd(e−eprev)/Δt. Use desired 4 rad/s, measured 3 rad/s, eprev=0.5 rad/s, Iprev=0.2 rad, Δt=0.1 s, Kp=0.2 s/rad, Ki=0.1/rad, Kd=0.01 s²/rad. What is unsaturated u?',['0.28.','0.23.','0.27.','0.325.'],'e=1, I=0.3 and derivative=5, so u=0.2+0.03+0.05=0.28.',['This omits the derivative contribution.','This uses the old integral0.2 instead of updated0.3.','This does not follow the stated error/integral/derivative convention.'],typ='numerical',difficulty='medium',assumptions=['Added algorithm and gains, not the robot’s unprinted implementation. Normalized command has no saturation in this question.'],steps=['e=4−3=1; I=0.2+1(0.1)=0.3.','de/dt≈(1−0.5)/0.1=5.','Sum P0.2, I0.03 and D0.05.'],forms=[PF])
add([(1888,'statement','Minimize error, compensate load, maintain stability objectives.','conflict')],'pid-limits','PID performance qualification','The slide lists stability and error reduction as PID objectives. With no gains, plant model or saturation data supplied, which conclusion is warranted?',['These are controller-design objectives; the slide alone does not establish stability or zero error for every load.','Any positive PID gains establish closed-loop stability for every motor/load.','Integral action prevents actuator saturation from affecting performance.','Encoder feedback makes parameter tuning unnecessary.'],'Performance depends on plant, tuning and constraints; a qualitative objective list is not a universal guarantee.',['Positive gains alone do not establish the full closed-loop dynamics.','Integral action does not remove physical actuator limits.','Feedback still requires an appropriate design and tuning.'],conflict='p1888 lists eliminating accumulated error and improving stability without gains or operating assumptions; retain these as objectives rather than unconditional guarantees.')
add([(1889,'table','map, odom, base_link, laser and camera_link definitions.')],'frames','Reference-frame roles','Which mapping matches the source frame table?',['map: global; odom: continuous odometry; base_link: robot body; laser/camera_link: sensor references.','map: camera pixel grid; odom: desired goal; base_link: global origin; laser: wheel axis.','map: wheel body; odom: camera optical frame; base_link: global map; camera_link: PWM frame.','map and odom: identical by definition; base_link: LiDAR-only frame.'],'The table assigns global, continuous local, body and sensor references separately.',['This confuses map/body/sensor references with task or pixel quantities.','These assignments contradict the table.','The source distinguishes map and odom, and base_link is the body frame.'])
TF=formula('Tmb=Tmo Tob; pmap=Rmb pbody+tmb',{'Tmb':'homogeneous transform expressing body coordinates in map','Tmo':'transform expressing odom coordinates in map','Tob':'transform expressing body coordinates in odom','Rmb':'body-to-map rotation','tmb':'map position of body origin','pmap,pbody':'same physical point expressed in map/body frames'},{'Tmb,Tmo,Tob':'rotation blocks dimensionless; translation entries m','Rmb':'dimensionless','tmb,pmap,pbody':'m'},['Added column-vector convention, homogeneous bottom row[0,0,1] in planar examples; multiplication order follows adjoining frame cancellation.'])
add([(1889,'figure','Top frame chain map → odom → base_link.')],'frame-order','Transform order','Define T_ab to map column-vector coordinates from frame b into frame a. Which expression follows map→odom→base_link?',['T_map,base=T_map,odom T_odom,base.','T_map,base=T_odom,base T_map,odom.','T_map,base=T_map,odom+T_odom,base.','T_map,base=T_map,odom T_base,odom.'],'The intermediate odom frame cancels in the ordered product.',['Rigid transforms generally do not commute.','Transform composition is multiplication, not elementwise addition.','The second factor has the inverse direction and does not join the chain.'],difficulty='medium',assumptions=['Explicit added column-vector T_ab convention.'],forms=[TF])
add([(1889,'figure','map → odom → base_link chain; numerical poses not provided.')],'frame-point','Planar point transformation','Added transforms: map←odom is a +90° planar rotation with translation (1,2) m; odom←base is identity rotation with translation (2,0) m. A point is (1,0) m in base. What is its map coordinate?',['(1,5) m.','(4,2) m.','(3,3) m.','(−1,5) m.'],'The point is (3,0) in odom; rotate it to(0,3), then translate to(1,5) in map.',['This adds translations without rotating the odom-coordinate point.','This rotates only the point but not the body-origin translation.','This introduces a sign error in the map x translation.'],typ='numerical',difficulty='medium',assumptions=['Added transforms; column-vector convention, counterclockwise positive angles.'],steps=['p_odom=(1,0)+(2,0)=(3,0).','R90 p_odom=(0,3).','Add map←odom translation(1,2).'],forms=[TF])
add([(1889,'statement','TF maintains spatial relationship between robot components.')],'tf-calibration','TF and calibration','A camera mount is physically shifted but its stored transform is not updated. Which statement follows?',['TF can consistently propagate the stored transform while transformed camera points are physically wrong.','TF automatically measures the new camera mount pose from the frame name.','Renaming camera_link to laser corrects the extrinsic calibration.','The map frame alone makes camera extrinsics irrelevant.'],'A transform framework manages supplied relationships; a changed physical calibration must be represented correctly.',['Frame names do not measure geometry.','Renaming does not repair geometry.','Camera-to-body geometry is needed to place its measurements in map coordinates.'],typ='scenario',difficulty='medium',assumptions=['Added mount-change fault; no self-calibration method is supplied.'])
add([(1890,'statement','Wheel drift, IMU long-term drift and measurement uncertainties.')],'fusion','Sensor-fusion motivation','Why combine wheel odometry and inertial information rather than assume either is exact?',['Their errors and limitations differ, so a suitably modeled estimator can use complementary information.','Wheel slip is directly measured and removed by every IMU sample.','An IMU provides an indefinitely drift-free absolute position without additional assumptions.','Adding sensor values arithmetically is equivalent to a covariance-aware EKF.'],'The slide motivates fusion using uncertainty and complementary limitations.',['An IMU sample does not automatically identify all wheel slip.','Inertial estimation can drift and does not by itself establish absolute position.','An estimator needs models and uncertainty handling, not an arbitrary sum.'])
add([(1890,'figure','Wheel odometry, IMU, RPLidar scan boxes feeding EKF.','conflict')],'ekf-boundary','Conceptual fusion versus implementation','What can be inferred from the source’s RPLidar scan→EKF schematic without unprinted configuration files?',['It expresses an intended information contribution; it does not specify message interfaces, preprocessing or the measurement model.','It proves raw range arrays are directly accepted by the exact configured filter with no conversion.','It specifies the filter covariance matrices and timestamp policy.','It proves LiDAR and odometry errors are statistically independent.'],'The diagram is conceptual and omits the interfaces and statistical model needed to reproduce an implementation.',['No raw-message subscription or conversion is printed.','No numerical covariance/timing configuration is printed.','Sensor independence is not established by a plus sign or arrow.'],conflict='p1890 draws raw-scan information into EKF but supplies no measurement interface or preprocessing; do not silently assert a particular implemented subscription.')
KF=formula('K=P/(P+R); x+=x−+K(z−x−); P+=(1−K)P',{'K':'scalar Kalman gain','P':'prior scalar state-estimate variance','R':'measurement-noise variance','x−,x+':'prior and posterior scalar position estimate','z':'independent scalar position observation','P+':'posterior variance'},{'K':'dimensionless','P,R,P+':'m²','x−,x+,z':'m'},['Added linear scalar measurement z=x+noise with H=1, independent unbiased errors and positive variances; illustration, not the robot’s unknown EKF configuration.'])
add([(1890,'statement','EKF fuses uncertain sensor measurements to estimate robot state.')],'fusion-number','Added uncertainty-weighted update','In an explicitly added scalar illustration, prior position is1.0 m with variance0.04 m², independent observation is1.3 m with variance0.01 m². Use K=P/(P+R). What are posterior position and variance?',['1.24 m and0.008 m².','1.15 m and0.025 m².','1.06 m and0.032 m².','1.30 m and0 m².'],'K=0.8, posterior=1+0.8(0.3)=1.24 and variance=(1−0.8)0.04=0.008.',['This substitutes an unweighted average and average variance.','This reverses the gain weighting.','A finite-noise observation does not make the estimate exact.'],typ='numerical',difficulty='medium',assumptions=['Added scalar H=1 linear Gaussian illustration; independent errors. Not a reproduction of source EKF code.'],steps=['K=0.04/(0.04+0.01)=0.8.','Apply the innovation0.3 m.','Compute posterior variance0.2×0.04.'],forms=[KF])
add([(1891,'table','LiDAR fixed scan plane versus RGB-D low/off-plane obstacles and narrower view.')],'off-plane','Complementary obstacle coverage','A low obstacle lies below the planar LiDAR scan but within the camera’s valid depth field of view. Which source-motivated response is appropriate?',['Use depth evidence in the local obstacle representation instead of treating the absent planar return as proof of free space.','Mark the obstacle free because the360° LiDAR has no return at its height.','Treat RGB colour class alone as a measured obstacle height.','Discard depth because the camera has a narrower field of view than LiDAR.'],'The camera can complement the fixed scan plane for low or off-plane obstacles, subject to valid depth coverage.',['360° angular coverage does not cover every vertical height.','A colour/class label alone is not metric depth or height.','Narrower view limits coverage but does not invalidate valid measurements within it.'],typ='scenario',difficulty='medium')
