add([(1891,'figure','Inflated obstacle bands around lethal/inscribed regions and local costmap flow.')],'inflation','Costmap clearance meaning','Why is a route that avoids only lethal cell centers insufficient to establish clearance for a finite-size robot?',['The robot footprint and safety margin can overlap nearby occupied space even when its centerline misses lethal cells.','Every nonlethal cell has exactly the same collision risk regardless of footprint.','A low-cost colour proves the robot can fit through any gap.','The camera’s RGB resolution alone defines the robot footprint.'],'Collision reasoning must account for the body’s extent and margins, reflected by regions around obstacles.',['Costs and footprint geometry matter beyond center cells.','A cost colour alone is not a geometric clearance proof.','Footprint is robot geometry, not camera pixel resolution.'],typ='scenario',difficulty='medium',assumptions=['Added finite-footprint interpretation of the displayed cost bands; no exact radius is printed.'])
